        "original_id": "4c78ea8d-5170-5c6d-b77f-e14a6b158a8c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: The Sports Museum, The Sports Museum of New England, BoSox Club\n- Places: TD Garden, Boston, Massachusetts\n- Systems: Boston Red Sox Hall of Fame selection committee\n- Topics: museum location, arena naming history, nomination process\n\nFacts:\n- TD Garden opened in 1995 in Boston, Massachusetts, as a replacement for the original Boston Garden.\n- TD Garden is a multi-purpose arena in Boston, Massachusetts, and it has also been known as Boston Garden, The Garden, Shawmut Center, FleetCenter, and TD Banknorth Garden.\n- The Sports Museum, also known as The Sports Museum of New England, is a non-profit museum currently located in TD Garden in Boston, Massachusetts.\n- A 15-member Boston Red Sox Hall of Fame selection committee nominates candidates, and the committee includes Red Sox broadcasters and executives, past and present media personnel, and representatives from The Sports Museum of New England and the BoSox Club.",
